.Dd September 23, 2026
.Dt ICOWM-THEME 5
.Os IcoWM 1.0.1
.Sh NAME
.Nm themes/name.json
.Nd theme file format for IcoWM
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A theme file describes the appearance of everything
.Xr icowm 1
draws: window frames and titlebars, desktop icons, the menus, the
dialogs, the system tray, the search box and the prompt.
.Pp
Themes live under
.Pa themes/
in the configuration directory, one file each, and the one to load is
named by
.Ic theme
in
.Xr icowm 5 ,
without the
.Ql .json
suffix.
Every key is optional: what a file leaves out keeps the built-in
default, so a theme need only state what it changes.
A key's case does not matter, nor does writing it with
.Ql -
or with
.Ql _ :
.Ic is-decorated ,
.Ic is_decorated
and
.Ic Is-Decorated
all name the same field.
.Pp
.Ic name
at the top level is the theme's own name, written to the debug log
when the theme loads and otherwise unused.
A key beginning with
.Ql -
or
.Ql _
is ignored, which is how
.Ic -author ,
.Ic -creation-date
and the like are written as comments.
.Ss Common shapes
Several shapes recur throughout, and are described once here:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic color
An object with
.Ic background
and
.Ic foreground ,
each a hex color as
.Ql #RRGGBB
or
.Ql RRGGBB ,
the leading
.Ql #
being optional.
.It Ic border
An object with
.Ic color ,
a hex color in the same
.Ql #RRGGBB
form, and
.Ic width ,
in pixels.
.It Ic padding
An object with
.Ic horizontal
and
.Ic vertical ,
in pixels.
.It Ic font
A string; see
.Sx Fonts
below.
.It Ic opacity
An integer from 0 to 100.
.Pp
Opacity is published on the window through
.Ql _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY
and nothing more.
.Xr icowm 1
never composites anything itself, so any value other than 100 has no
visible effect whatever unless a compositing manager, such as
.Xr picom 1 ,
is also running and reading the property back.
Without one, a theme may set this freely and nothing on screen will
change.
.El
.Ss Sections
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic window
The frame around an ordinary window.
.Ic active
and
.Ic inactive
each hold a
.Ic color ,
a
.Ic border ,
a
.Ic font
and an
.Ic opacity ,
for the focused window and the rest.
.Ic titlebar
holds its
.Ic height ,
zero being equivalent to
.Ic is-decorated
set false, its text
.Ic alignment ,
one of
.Ql left
(the default),
.Ql center
or
.Ql right ,
its
.Ic padding ,
and a
.Ic buttons
object naming which buttons sit
.Ic left
and which
.Ic right ,
with a
.Ic color
having
.Ic on
and
.Ic off
for pressed and idle.
Both lists take the same nine names, in the order they are to be drawn,
outwards from their own edge of the titlebar:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ql pin
Keep the window on every desktop.
.It Ql sticky
Keep the window on every viewport page.
.It Ql layer
Move the window between the below, normal and above layers.
.It Ql shade
Roll the window up into its own titlebar.
.It Ql iconize
Send the window to its desktop icon.
.It Ql hide
Take the window out of view without iconifying it.
.It Ql maximize
Grow the window to fill its work area.
.It Ql fullscreen
Grow the window to fill the whole screen, decorations included.
.It Ql close
Ask the window to close.
.El
A name the list does not recognize is ignored, and a list may hold at
most
.Dv CONFIG_MAX_TITLEBAR_BUTTONS
entries.
A button whose action makes no sense for the stage it is on is left
out on its own: the
.Ql pin
button on a single-desktop stage, the
.Ql sticky
button where the viewport has one page.
.Ic buttons.size
is the side of one button in pixels, chosen here rather than derived
from
.Ic height :
making the titlebar taller is a decision about the bar and does not
resize the buttons in it.
It is held to at least six pixels, to at most the titlebar height less
two, and rounded down to an even number.
.Ic buttons.use-symbols
decides whether each button draws the symbol of its own action,
crossed diagonals for
.Ic close
and so on, or whether every button is the plain filled square that
.Ic pin , Ic sticky
and
.Ic layer
are either way.
.Ic is-decorated
decides whether a window is framed at all by default.
.It Ic icon
A desktop icon, in the same
.Ic active
and
.Ic inactive
shape.
.Ic is-captioned
decides whether the window name is shown beneath it, and
.Ic show-hints
and
.Ic show-pixmaps
whether the icon comes from the window's own hints and pixmaps.
.It Ic cycle
The frame drawn around the window being cycled to, through
.Ic border .
.It Ic systray
The tray's own
.Ic color ,
.Ic border ,
.Ic font ,
.Ic opacity
and
.Ic height ,
plus
.Ic pixmap
with the
.Ic size
of a docked icon and the
.Ic padding
around it, and
.Ic text
with the
.Ic gap
before the clock and its vertical
.Ic valign ,
one of
.Ql top ,
.Ql bottom
or
.Ql center
(the default).
.It Ic desktop
The desktop background, through
.Ic color .
.It Ic menu
.Ic unselected ,
.Ic selected
and
.Ic label
each hold a
.Ic color ,
a
.Ic border
and a
.Ic font ,
for an ordinary row, the one under the pointer, and a heading.
.Ic disabled
holds
.Ic color.foreground
for a row that cannot be chosen; unlike the shape's usual
.Ic background
and
.Ic foreground
pair, only
.Ic foreground
is read here.
.Ic separator
the
.Ic color
of a dividing line, and the section itself a
.Ic border ,
a
.Ic padding ,
an
.Ic opacity
and
.Ic show-pixmaps .
.It Ic dialog
.Ic color.background
and
.Ic border
for the dialog itself, only
.Ic background
being read out of the usual color pair,
.Ic opacity ,
.Ic label
for its text, holding a
.Ic font ,
a
.Ic padding
and a
.Ic color.foreground
(again only
.Ic foreground ,
not the full pair), and
.Ic button
holding the
.Ic gap
between buttons, their
.Ic padding ,
and a
.Ic selected
and
.Ic unselected
style each.
.It Ic overlay
The small box reporting a geometry during a drag, through
.Ic color ,
.Ic border ,
.Ic font
and
.Ic opacity .
.It Ic search
The window search box:
.Ic input
for the field,
.Ic selected
and
.Ic unselected
for its rows, and a
.Ic border .
.It Ic prompt
The command box:
.Ic label ,
.Ic input
and a
.Ic border .
.It Ic scratchpad
The scratchpad window's own
.Ic border .
.It Ic xsettings
What is published to XSettings-aware toolkits:
.Ic is-enabled ,
a
.Ic dpi ,
and a
.Ic theme
object naming
.Ic gtk-theme-name ,
.Ic icon-theme-name ,
.Ic cursor-theme-name
and
.Ic cursor-theme-size .
This changes nothing about what
.Xr icowm 1
itself draws; it only tells other applications what to use.
.El
.Ss Fonts
Every
.Ic font
field takes the same kind of string, tried through two backends in
order.
.Pp
X core fonts are tried first, through XCB.
Only X11 bitmap fonts, BDF and PCF, are reachable this way; it goes
first because it costs nothing per glyph and every X server ships the
.Ql fixed
family.
A short description such as
.Ql \&"fixed bold 13\&"
almost always takes this path.
.Pp
Anything that does not resolve as an X core font is tried through
fontconfig for matching, FreeType for rasterizing and the X RENDER
extension for compositing.
A family name such as
.Ql \&"DejaVu Sans\&" ,
which most systems have only as a scalable font, takes this path, and
uses fontconfig's own pattern syntax.
This is what gives real anti-aliasing and full UTF-8, neither of which
the core font path can provide.
.Pp
No field or prefix selects the backend: it is decided purely by whether
the string resolves as an X core font first.
A string resolving through neither falls back to
.Ql fixed ,
so one bad value never leaves text unrenderable.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/icowm/themes/
Where theme files live, at the first of the several locations
.Xr icowm 1
looks in.
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/icowm/themes/default.json
The theme shipped with
.Xr icowm 1 .
The same values are built into the binary, so a session with no theme
file still looks like this; the two differ only in the name they
report,
.Ql Default (built-in)
when the values come from the binary.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A theme that changes only its window colors, everything else keeping
the built-in default:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "name": "slate",
    "-author": "Jane Doe",

    "window": {
        "active": {
            "color": {
                "background": "#9AAEC8",
                "foreground": "#1B222E"
            },
            "font": "fixed bold"
        },
        "inactive": {
            "color": {
                "background": "#D0D9E5",
                "foreground": "#3A4351"
            },
            "font": "fixed"
        }
    }
}
.Ed
.Pp
A theme asking for a scalable font, which takes the fontconfig path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "name": "sans",
    "window": {
        "active": { "font": "DejaVu Sans:weight=bold:size=11" },
        "inactive": { "font": "DejaVu Sans:size=11" }
    }
}
.Ed
